WEBVTT

00:52:27.367 --> 00:52:30.368
CA: I mean, is there any political policy

00:52:30.392 --> 00:52:34.694
that could further empower and inspire
more people to join that movement?

00:52:34.718 --> 00:52:37.361
DB: You know, the politics,
as I say, comes last.

00:52:37.385 --> 00:52:38.740
There are things I would do.

00:52:38.764 --> 00:52:43.063
One thing I would do is I would take
the charitable tax credit

00:52:43.087 --> 00:52:45.837
and I would make it possible
as a refundable credit

00:52:45.861 --> 00:52:49.270
for people who are not making enough
to really itemize their deductions,

00:52:49.294 --> 00:52:52.501
to really encourage charitable giving
up and down the income stream,

00:52:52.525 --> 00:52:53.689
or at least reward it.

00:52:53.713 --> 00:52:55.241
The giving is already happening.

00:52:55.265 --> 00:52:58.576
Poor people give a higher percentage
of their income than rich people.

00:52:58.600 --> 00:53:02.205
CA: You get a deduction
even if you're not paying taxes?